## Bug: Tool calls fail with `unknown tool ""` (empty name) when a large tool call is split into multiple stream chunks

### Environment
- DeepSeek Harness `0.1.0-rc.6` (npm @deepseek-ai/dsh)
- Provider: `deepseek-official` route → opencode-go gateway (`https://opencode.ai/zen/go/v1`), model `deepseek-v4-flash`
- Agent preset: standard, permission: danger-full-access

### Symptom
After a tool call whose `arguments` are split across many SSE chunks, **every subsequent tool call fails with** `Error: unknown tool ""` (`ToolNotFoundError`, code `UNKNOWN_TOOL`). This is systemic, not per-tool: `bash`, `grep`, `read`, `echo`, `web_search` all fail. Once it starts it never recovers in the same step; the session is effectively dead for tool use.

### Root cause (confirmed with raw stream bytes)
In `packages/llm/llm/src/assembler.ts` (`BlockAssembler`), two defects combine:

1. **`tool-call-delta` id capture is unconditional** — it clobbers the first-captured id:
   ```ts
   partial.toolCallId = chunk.id;                    // unconditional: later empty-id deltas reset it
   if (chunk.name) partial.toolCallName = chunk.name; // guarded — name survives, id does not
   ```
   When the gateway emits an empty `id` on subsequent deltas, `partial.toolCallId` becomes `''`.

2. **`block-end` + `assemble()` short-circuit discards the accumulated name/id** even when they *were* correctly captured:
   ```ts
   case 'block-end': {
       ...
       partial.block = chunk.block;   // raw block (may carry empty name/id) overwrites
   }
   assemble(partial, index) {
       if (partial.block) return partial.block;  // returns raw block as-is; accumulated deltas ignored
   }
   ```
   So even when `partial.toolCallName` was set correctly, `assemble()` returns the raw `block-end` block whose `name`/`id` may be empty → `ToolNotFoundError: unknown tool ""`.

### Evidence (raw chunks from a failed session)
A failing `bash` call, same block index, name present on the first delta only, then all-empty `id`/`name`; the `block-end` carries an empty block:
```json
{"type":"assistant/chunk","data":{"chunk":{"type":"tool-call-delta","index":2,"id":"call_2a60dd...","name":"bash","argumentsDelta":""}}}
{"type":"assistant/chunk","data":{"chunk":{"type":"tool-call-delta","index":2,"id":"","name":null,"argumentsDelta":"{"}}}
{"type":"assistant/chunk","data":{"chunk":{"type":"tool-call-delta","index":2,"id":"","name":null,"argumentsDelta":"\"command\": ..."}}}
... many more deltas, all id="" name=null, argumentsDelta only ...
{"type":"assistant/chunk","data":{"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":2,"block":{"type":"tool-call","name":"","id":"","arguments":"{...full args...}"}}}}
```
Contrast a healthy call where **every** delta carries `name`:
```json
{"type":"assistant/chunk","data":{"chunk":{"type":"tool-call-delta","index":1,"id":"call_00_...","name":"job_list","argumentsDelta":"{}"}}}
```

### Trigger condition
A **single tool call whose `arguments` are split into many stream chunks** (large/full-content arguments — e.g. a big file read or long command). The gateway emits `name`/`id` only on the first delta; when the *(non-deterministic)* chunk-split boundary separates the name-bearing delta from the argument deltas, the assembler drops the name. This is why it appears "random" and reproduces across fresh sessions and restarts.

### Minimal reproduction
```ts
import { BlockAssembler } from '@deepseek-ai/dsh-llm';

// Simulates the gateway's large-tool-call split: first delta carries id+name,
// subsequent deltas carry only arguments (id="", name=null), block-end is empty.
const a = new BlockAssembler();
a.push({ type: 'block-start', index: 0, blockType: 'tool-call' });
a.push({ type: 'tool-call-delta', index: 0, id: 'call_2a60dd', name: 'bash', argumentsDelta: '' });
a.push({ type: 'tool-call-delta', index: 0, id: '', name: null, argumentsDelta: '{"command": "echo hi"}' });
a.push({ type: 'tool-call-delta', index: 0, id: '', name: null, argumentsDelta: '' });
a.push({ type: 'block-end', index: 0, block: { type: 'tool-call', name: '', id: '', arguments: '' } });
console.log(JSON.stringify(a.blocks()));
// Expected: name returns as 'bash' with id and arguments.
// Actual (rc.6): name='' id='' → ToolNotFoundError: unknown tool "".
```

### Suggested fix
Make `assemble()` treat the accumulated deltas as authoritative for any field the raw `block-end` block is missing:
```ts
assemble(partial, index) {
    if (partial.block) {
        let block = partial.block;
        if (!block.name && partial.toolCallName) block = { ...block, name: partial.toolCallName };
        if (!block.id && partial.toolCallId)     block = { ...block, id: partial.toolCallId };
        if (!block.arguments && partial.toolCallArguments) block = { ...block, arguments: partial.toolCallArguments };
        return block;
    }
    ...
}
```
and guard the id capture to match name (`if (chunk.id) partial.toolCallId = chunk.id;`).

The assembler already documents "log the raw chunks for replay fidelity" — the accumulated `partial.*` values are provably correct here, so backfilling is safe and cannot regress the healthy path (verified: a fully-populated `block-end` is returned unchanged).

### Notes
- Fix verified against the raw failing stream and the minimal repro above (3-field backfill: name, id, arguments).
- `rc.7` (`0.1.0-rc.7`) does **not** fix this: commit `84257ea` changes only max-tokens replay-metadata alignment; `assemble()` still short-circuits on `partial.block`.

