Some OAuth-protected MCP servers require a pre-registered loopback redirect URI. The current client configuration exposes a callback port but uses a fixed callback path. This prevents otherwise compatible public clients from completing authorization when their registered path differs.

Could streamable HTTP MCP configuration support an optional callback path for each server while keeping the current default? The callback listener should validate against the configured path. This would keep the current dynamic-registration flow and allow exact redirect-URI matching for pre-registered OAuth clients.

I would be happy to test an upstream implementation.

